{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-intro","title":"Mark 1 — Chapter Introduction","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":0,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":0},"content":"<p>and made.Every thing was here done which human policy and prudence could, to prevent a resurrection, which these very precautions had the most direct tendency to authenticate and establish.</p>\n<p>sealing. Da 6:17; 2Ti 2:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-1","title":"Mark 1:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The office of John the Baptist. 9 Jesus is baptized; 12 tempted; 14 he preaches; 16 calls Peter, Andrew, James, and John; 23 heals one that had a devil; 29 Peter's mother in law; 32 many diseased persons; 40 and cleanses the leper.</p>\n<p>beginning. Lu 1:2,3; 2:10,11; Ac 1:1,2 Christ. Joh 20:31; Ro 1:1-4; 1Jo 1:1-3; 5:11,12 son. Ps 2:7; Mt 3:17; 14:33; 17:5; Lu 1:35; Joh 1:14,34,49; 3:16; 6:69 Ro 8:3,32; Heb 1:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-2","title":"Mark 1:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>written. Ps 40:7; Mt 2:5; 26:24,31; Lu 1:70; 18:31 in.Several MSS. have, \"by Isaiah the prophet.\" See the parallel texts.</p>\n<p>Behold. Mal 3:1; Mt 11:10; Lu 1:15-17,76; 7:27,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-3","title":"Mark 1:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Isa 40:3-5; Mt 3:3; Lu 3:4-6; Joh 1:15,19-34; 3:28-36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-4","title":"Mark 1:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>did. Mt 3:1,2,6,11; Lu 3:2,3; Joh 3:23; Ac 10:37; 13:24,25; 19:3,4 for. or, unto. remission. Ac 22:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-5","title":"Mark 1:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>there. Mt 3:5,6; 4:25 baptized. Joh 1:28; 3:23 confessing. Le 26:40-42; Jos 7:19; Ps 32:5; Pr 28:13; Ac 2:38; 19:18 1Jo 1:8-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-6","title":"Mark 1:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>clothed. 2Ki 1:8; Zec 13:4; Mt 3:4 eat. Le 11:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-7","title":"Mark 1:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Mt 3:11,14; Lu 3:16; 7:6,7; Joh 1:27; 3:28-31; Ac 13:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-8","title":"Mark 1:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>have. Mt 3:11 he shall. Pr 1:23; Isa 32:15; 44:3; Eze 36:25-27; Joe 2:28; Ac 1:5; 2:4,17 Ac 10:45; 11:15,16; 19:4-6; 1Co 12:13; Tit 3:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-9","title":"Mark 1:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>that. Mt 3:13-15; Lu 3:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-10","title":"Mark 1:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>coming. Mt 3:16; Joh 1:31-34 opened. or, cloven. or rent. Isa 64:1 the Spirit. Isa 42:1; Lu 3:22; Joh 1:32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-11","title":"Mark 1:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>there. Mt 3:17; Joh 5:37; 12:28-30; 2Pe 1:17,18 Thou. 9:7; Ps 2:7; Isa 42:1; Mt 17:5; Lu 9:35; Joh 1:34; 3:16,35,36 Joh 5:20-23; 6:69; Ro 1:4; Col 1:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-12","title":"Mark 1:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>the Spirit. Mt 4:1-11; Lu 4:1-4 driveth.Or, \"sendeth him forth,\" [ekballo auton.] The expression does not necessarily imply any violence; but seems to intimate the energy of that impulse on our Lord, by which he was inwardly constrained to retire from society.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-13","title":"Mark 1:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>forty. Ex 24:18; 34:28; De 9:11,18,25; 1Ki 19:8 tempted. Heb 2:17,18; 4:15 and the. 1Ki 19:5-7; Mt 4:11; 26:53; 1Ti 3:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-14","title":"Mark 1:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>A.M. 4031. A.D. 27. after. Mt 4:12; 11:2; 14:2; Lu 3:20; Joh 3:22-24 preaching. Isa 61:1-3; Mt 4:23; 9:35; Lu 4:17-19,43,44; 8:1; Ac 20:25; 28:23 Eph 2:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-15","title":"Mark 1:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>The time. Da 2:44; 9:25; Ga 4:4; Eph 1:10 the kingdom. Mt 3:2; 4:17; 10:7; Lu 10:9,11 repent. Mt 21:31,32; Lu 24:47; Ac 2:36-38; 20:21; 2Ti 2:25,26 believe. Ro 16:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-16","title":"Mark 1:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>as he. Mt 4:18-22; Lu 5:1,4-11 Simon. 3:16,18; Mt 10:2; Lu 6:14; Joh 1:40-42; 6:8; 12:22; Ac 1:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-17","title":"Mark 1:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>fishers. Eze 47:10; Mt 4:19,20; Lu 5:10; Ac 2:38-41</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-18","title":"Mark 1:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>forsook. 10:28-31; Mt 19:27-30; Lu 5:11; 14:33; 18:28-30; Php 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-19","title":"Mark 1:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>James. 3:17; 5:37; 9:2; 10:35; 14:33; Mt 4:21; Ac 1:13; 12:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-20","title":"Mark 1:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>they left. 10:29; De 33:9; 1Ki 19:20; Mt 4:21,22; 8:21,22; 10:37; Lu 14:26 2Co 5:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-21","title":"Mark 1:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>they went. 2:1; Mt 4:13; Lu 4:31; 10:15 Capernaum.Capernaum was a city of Galilee, (Lu 4:31,) situated on the confines of Zebulun, and Naphtali, (Mt 4:13,) on the western border of the lake of Tiberias, (Joh 6:59,) and in the land of Gennesaret, (ch. 6:53; Mt 14:34,) where Josephus places a spring of excellent water called Capernaum. Dr. Lightfoot places it between Tiberias and Tarichea, about two miles from the former; and Dr. Richardson, in passing through the plain of Gennesaret, was told by the natives that the ruins of Capernaum were quite near. The Arab station and ruins mentioned by Mr. Buckingham, said to have been formerly called Capharnaoom, situated on the edge of the lake from nine to twelve miles N. N. E. of Tiberias, bearing the name of Talhewn, or as Burckhardt writes it, Tel Houm, appear too far north for its site.</p>\n<p>he entered. 39; 6:2; Mt 4:23; Lu 4:16; 13:10; Ac 13:14-52; 17:2; 18:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-22","title":"Mark 1:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>they were. Jer 23:29; Mt 7:28,29; 13:54; Lu 4:32; 21:15; Joh 7:46; Ac 6:10 Ac 9:21,22; 2Co 4:2; Heb 4:12,13 as the. 7:3-13; Mt 23:16-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-23","title":"Mark 1:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>a man. 34; 5:2; 7:25; 9:25; Mt 12:43; Lu 4:33-37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-24","title":"Mark 1:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Let. 5:7; Ex 14:12; Mt 8:29; Lu 8:28,37; Jas 2:19 the Holy One. Ps 16:10; 89:18,19; Da 9:24; Lu 4:34; Ac 2:27; 3:14; 4:27; Re 3:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-25","title":"Mark 1:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>rebuked. 34; 3:11,12; 9:25; Ps 50:16; Lu 4:35,41; Ac 16:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-26","title":"Mark 1:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>torn. 9:20,26; Lu 9:39,42; 11:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-27","title":"Mark 1:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>they were. 7:37; Mt 9:33; 12:22,23; 15:31 for. Lu 4:36; 9:1; 10:17-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-28","title":"Mark 1:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>45; Mic 5:4; Mt 4:24; 9:31; Lu 4:17,37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-29","title":"Mark 1:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>entered. Mt 8:14,15; Lu 4:38,39; 9:58</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-30","title":"Mark 1:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>wife's. 1Co 9:5 they tell. 5:23; Joh 11:3; Jas 5:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-31","title":"Mark 1:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>and took. 5:41; Ac 9:41 ministered. 15:41; Ps 103:1-3; 116:12; Mt 27:55; Lu 8:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-32","title":"Mark 1:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>at even. 21; 3:2; Mt 8:16; Lu 4:40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-33","title":"Mark 1:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>5; Ac 13:44</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-34","title":"Mark 1:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>and suffered. 25; 3:12; Lu 4:41; Ac 16:16-18 speak, because they. or, say that they.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-35","title":"Mark 1:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>6:46-48; Ps 5:3; 109:4; Lu 4:42; 6:12; 22:39-46; Joh 4:34; 6:15 Eph 6:18; Php 2:5; Heb 5:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-37","title":"Mark 1:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>All. 5; Zec 11:11; Joh 3:26; 11:48; 12:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-38","title":"Mark 1:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>Let. Lu 4:43 for. Isa 61:1-3; Lu 2:49; 4:18-21; Joh 9:4; 16:28; 17:4,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-39","title":"Mark 1:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>preached. 21; Mt 4:23; Lu 4:43,44 Galilee.Galilee was a province of Palestine, being bounded, says Josephus, on the west by Ptolemais and mount Carmel; on the south by the country of Samaria and Scythopolis, on the river Jordan; on the east by the cantons of Hyppos, Gadara, and Gaulon; and on the north by the confines of the Tyrians. It was divided into Lower and Upper Galilee;--Upper Galilee, so called from its being mountainous, was termed Galilee of the Gentiles (Mt 4:15,) because inhabited, says Strabo, by Egyptians, Arabians, and Phoenicians, and comprehended the tribes of Asher and Naphtali; the Lower Galilee contained the tribes of Zebulun and Issachar, and was sometimes termed the Great Field. It was, says Josephus, very populous and rich, containing 204 cities and towns.</p>\n<p>and cast. 7:30; Lu 4:41</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-40","title":"Mark 1:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>there. Mt 8:2-4; Lu 5:12-14 a leper. Le 13:1-14:57; Nu 12:10-15; De 24:8,9; 2Sa 3:29; 2Ki 5:5-27 2Ki 5:27; 7:3; 15:5; Mt 11:5; Lu 17:12-19 kneeling. 10:17; 2Ch 6:13; Mt 17:14; Lu 22:41; Ac 7:60; Eph 3:14 if thou. 9:22,23; Ge 18:14; 2Ki 5:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-41","title":"Mark 1:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>moved. 6:34; Mt 9:36; Lu 7:12,13; Heb 2:17; 4:15 I. 4:39; 5:41; Ge 1:3; Ps 33:9; Heb 1:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-42","title":"Mark 1:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>immediately. 31; 5:29; Ps 33:9; Mt 15:28; Joh 4:50-53; 15:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-43","title":"Mark 1:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>3:12; 5:43; 7:36; Mt 9:30; Lu 8:56</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-44","title":"Mark 1:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>shew. Le 14:2-32; Mt 23:2,3; Lu 5:14; 17:14 for a testimony. Ro 15:4; 1Co 10:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-1-45","title":"Mark 1:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>and began. Ps 77:11; Mt 9:31; Lu 5:15; Tit 1:10 could. 2:1,2,13</p>"}]}